    LLM: "Last to play has advantage (voir venir); first two often play low, third may play high, fourth beats or spoils. Spoil to keep lead with partner.\n\nSignal only when partner needs the information; avoid signalling when your hand is strong (helps opponents). Support partner's mordienne by spoiling and spreading tricks.\n\nSurrender offer and mordienne commitment; announced mordienne (variant) extends match to 10 points.",
